{
  "meta": {
    "name_ar": "فهرس العوامل وسلاسل المواضع",
    "name_en": "Index of awamil (governors) and entry-chains for each position",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "purpose_en": "Every 'aamil in one table: what it governs, with which i'rab effect, its members, and an example. The 'chains' section answers: 'what can come onto this position?' — e.g. onto the mubtada: kana-group (raises it), inna-group (makes it accusative), zann/verbs of hearts (makes it accusative as first object), and the no-op entrants (lolla, lawma, lām al-ibtidā', lā an-nāfiya lil-jins). Sentences in sentences.json carry an \"awamil\" array of these ids, so you can filter the corpus by any 'aamil: python3 nahw/tarkeeb.py awamil <id>",
